**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Every parameter name an item model publishes is written once, as a member of `ParameterName`, so the evaluator of this section reads a value under the very name the model publishes (001 §I 'Each model publishes its parameter axes'; 001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a re-transcribed constant is a defect). No name's text, order, kind or default changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`, on `ParameterName` (moved there by step 205), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: static members answering the names steps 207, 208 and 215 publish, their texts unchanged: `azimuth`, `ellipticity`, `degreeOfPolarization` and `intensityScale` (the light source); `extinctionRatio`, `diattenuation` and `axisOffset` (the real linear polarizer); `retardance` and `fastAxisOffset` (the retarder plate); `blackBoxScale`, whose text is `scale` (the black box's scale); `gain` and `darkOffset` (the intensity detector); `rotationUncertainty`, `elementUncertainty` and `throughputUncertainty` (the noise budget); `dialZero` (a dial-mounted item); and `substrateThickness`, whose text is `substrate.thickness`. Static members over positions: `muellerElement (row : int) (column : int)` is `m<row><column>`, rows and columns 0 to 3 as step 208 numbers them; `filmThickness (position : int)` is `film<k>.thickness`; `repeatedLayerThickness (position : int) (layer : int)` is `film<k>.layer<j>.thickness`, both 1-based as step 207 numbers them. `member this.inComponent (position : int) : ParameterName` is the name prefixed `c<k>.` (1-based, light order), so a compound inside a compound prefixes twice. These are members, and a member may speak its type's own primitives (AGENTS.md 'Members may speak their type's own primitives'), so the positions stay `int`. (2) The publishers name the members and change nothing else. `SourcePreset` gains `static member lightSourceAxes : ItemParameterAxis list`, the four light-source axes of step 207 in their order with their kinds and defaults (`azimuth` and `ellipticity` `AngleParameter` 0, `degreeOfPolarization` `FractionParameter` 0, `intensityScale` `ScaleParameter` 1), and step 207's `SourcePreset.parameterAxes` answers it, so a run with no bound source reads the same default parameter set (step 252). `ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes` and `Sample.parameterAxes` (steps 206, 207), and `OpticalForm.parameterAxes` and `ItemModelForm.parameterAxes` (step 208), build every name through these members, a compound's prefix through `inComponent`. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, `ItemDial.parameterAxes` (step 215) names `ParameterName.dialZero`. No publisher writes a published name's text any more, and no other member, type or option is added. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests` (step 205): `every published parameter name is one ParameterName member`: `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` names `ParameterName.azimuth`, `ParameterName.ellipticity`, `ParameterName.degreeOfPolarization` and `ParameterName.intensityScale` in that order and equals `(BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633).parameterAxes`; `ParameterName.degreeOfPolarization.value` is `degreeOfPolarization`; `(ParameterName.muellerElement 2 3).value` is `m23`; `(ParameterName.filmThickness 2).value` is `film2.thickness`; `(ParameterName.repeatedLayerThickness 2 1).value` is `film2.layer1.thickness`; `ParameterName.substrateThickness.value` is `substrate.thickness`; `ParameterName.blackBoxScale.value` is `scale`; `(ParameterName.retardance.inComponent 2).value` is `c2.retardance`; and `((ParameterName.extinctionRatio.inComponent 1).inComponent 2).value` is `c2.c1.extinctionRatio`. Every fact of steps 207, 208 and 215 runs unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the names land, every parameter name an item model publishes MUST be one `ParameterName` member that the publishers name, every text, order, kind and default unchanged, and `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` MUST hold the four light-source axes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every published parameter name is one ParameterName member`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.
